e ideal of individual liberty, of the Louisiana Purchase, of the Lewis and Clark expedition, and of the settling of the West, Jefferson recognized that the genius of humanity, and the genius of the new nation, lay in the possibility of progress. Philosophers think; politicians maneuver. Jefferson's genius was that he was both and could do both, often simultaneously, catapulting him into becoming the most successful political leader of the early republic, and perhaps in all of American history."},"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"title":"Thomas Jefferson","subtitle":"the art of power","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1516333A"}],"publish_date":"2012","covers":[7248434,7246081],"lc_classifications":["E332 .M48 2012","E332.M48 2012"],"ocaid":"thomasjeffersona00meac","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i17.records.utf8:14230176:851","ia:thomasjeffersona00meac","marc:marc_openlibraries_phillipsacademy/PANO_FOR_IA_05072019.mrc:45007318:3921","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run04.mrc:268553593:4555","bwb:9781400067664","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part39.utf8:187719492:898","ia:thomasjeffersona0000meac","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-021.mrc:27779785:3925","marc:marc_nuls/NULS_PHC_180925.mrc:61479764:4644","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2024-07-15:W9-AWI-884","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:563073034:4409","midcolumbia:1108974","bwb:9780679645368","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_036.bib.mrc:199733290:5451","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2026-04-13:C0-BNH-403"],"edition_name":"1st ed.","subjects":["Politics and government","Presidents","Biography"],"subject_people":["Thomas Jefferson (1743-1826)"],"publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"Jon Meacham","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publishers":["Random House"],"physical_format":"Hardcover","fu